; Tutorial_8_Ask_About_a_File.inix -- a question about a file, answered on this computer.

[about]
Title=8 - Ask About a File
Intro=One want: what is in a long document, without reading it all. Shift plus F12 asks a model on this computer a question with the file's text attached; F12 asks a question about nothing in particular. The same keys as EdSharp.
Setup=A model is installed for FileDir's AI commands, and a folder holds a long document.
Homework=Ask Shift plus F12 to list the dates in a document of your own.


[step]

Say=One want: to know what is in a long report before deciding to read it. FileDir can ask a language model running on this computer, so nothing leaves it.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus F opens FileDir on the folder it last showed.
Key=Alt+Control+F
Hear=FileDir

[step]

Say=I arrow to the report. Shift plus F12 is Chat about File: the question travels with the file's text, converted from whatever it is, so a Word file or a PDF works as well as text.
Key=Shift+F12
Hear=Chat about File dialog
Hear=Question: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type the question.
Key=Summarize this in three sentences.
Hear=(each word echoed as it is typed)

[step]

Say=Enter asks.
Key=Enter
Hear=Answer dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The answer opens in a window, in a box I can arrow through line by line. Down Arrow reads the first line.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=(the first line of the answer)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus C copies a selection, and Escape, Enter or the Spacebar leaves, whichever is nearest the hand.
Key=Escape
Hear=FileDir
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: F12 without Shift is Chat with AI, which attaches nothing. Asking it to summarize this gets an answer about nothing in particular. Shift is what brings the file along.
Key=F12
Hear=Chat with AI dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes it unasked.
Key=Escape
Hear=FileDir
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Not every question needs a model. Control plus Shift plus T, Type Extended, lists every property FileDir can find for the file, alphabetically: its dates, its size, its author and title.
Key=Control+Shift+T
Hear=Type Extended, read only edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape returns to the list.
Key=Escape
Hear=FileDir
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=And the question mark, Say What Content, reads the file's own text aloud, or lists what is inside it if it is an archive.
Key=Question
Hear=Quarterly report. Summary. Revenue rose by 8 percent.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=When reading is not enough, the model can do what reading cannot: compare, summarize, pick out the dates or the names.
Key=

[step]

Say=A good question is a specific one. Shift plus F12 again, this time asking for every deadline in the report.
Key=Shift+F12
Hear=Chat about File dialog
Hear=Question: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type the question.
Key=List every deadline in this report, with its date.
Hear=(each word echoed as it is typed)

[step]

Say=Enter. The answer is a list, one deadline to a line, ready to copy into a calendar.
Key=Enter
Hear=Answer dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The model runs on this computer, through Ollama, so the report never leaves it. The first answer can be slow while the model loads; later ones are quicker.
Key=

[step]

Say=F12 has its own uses, for questions about nothing on disk: what a word means, how to phrase a sentence, what a file extension is for.
Key=F12
Hear=Chat with AI dialog
Hear=Question: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I ask what an EPUB file is.
Key=What is an EPUB file?
Hear=(each word echoed as it is typed)

[step]

Say=Enter, and the answer opens in the same kind of window as before.
Key=Enter
Hear=Answer dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus A selects the whole answer, and Control plus C copies it, to paste wherever it is needed.
Key=Control+A
Hear=selected
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the step; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Ask about the file I am on.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F12

[step]

Say=Ask a question about nothing in particular.
Key=
Hear=F12
